# CMB Power Spectrum bootstrap catalogue (Planck 2018 TT, representative slice).
# Each line below is one MPR row data block (NDJSON).
# Lines starting with "#" or empty lines are skipped by the
# literature_curated adapter.
#
# Single row_type "multipole_bin" catalogue (15 rows): TT-only representative
# slice spanning ℓ=2-2000, covering the qualitative features:
#   - low-ℓ Sachs-Wolfe plateau (incl. suppressed quadrupole anomaly)
#   - rising-to-first-peak regime
#   - first / second / third acoustic peaks
#   - first / second troughs
#   - damping tail onset and Silk-damping suppression
#
# Values are quoted to 2 significant figures from Planck 2018 VI
# (Aghanim et al. 2020, A&A 641:A6, doi:10.1051/0004-6361/201833910)
# — specifically Fig. 1 (binned D_ℓ TT plot) and Sec. 2 narrative.
# precision_flag = "rounded_2sf" reflects this; follow-up commit will
# ingest the full ~215-band PR3 Plik / Commander tables from the
# Planck Legacy Archive (https://pla.esac.esa.int/) and upgrade to
# "high" precision with proper likelihood errors.
#
# Error bars are cosmic-variance-floor estimates (σ_D_ℓ / D_ℓ ≈
# sqrt(2 / (2ℓ + 1) / (2·half_width + 1))) — the lower bound any
# binned measurement can achieve. Planck's actual likelihood errors
# at high ℓ include additional instrumental + foreground contributions
# (~ +30% beyond cosmic variance). Conservative for seed; will be
# replaced with PR3-likelihood errors in follow-up ingest.

